<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Egyptian Condominium</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Anglo-Egyptian Sudan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Egyptian Condominium was the arrangement by which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> was jointly ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 1899 until 1956, with Britain holding effective power. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-dinar">Ali Dinar</a> initially kept considerable autonomy. In 1916 a British expedition conquered Darfur and incorporated it into Anglo-Egyptian Sudan, ending the Darfur Sultanate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-egyptian-condominium.jpg" alt="Anglo-Egyptian Condominium" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Acts of Union 1800 Vector: Yaddah · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_(3-5).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
